{
 "tableDesc": "70 tasks in two tiers, run at pass@1 over the same browser tool. The **core tier** (27 tasks) is deterministic browser-control work every configuration should pass: forms and multi-page flows, table editing and validation, triage and scheduling, keyboard-only and hover-only UIs, precision clicks, iframes and nested scrolling, and read-only GitHub and Wikipedia navigation. The **discriminating tier** (43 tasks) holds tasks that at least one frontier configuration failed on both of two attempts during construction: 29 are counting and tracking over rendered video clips, the rest are exact visual counting, tracing and real-site judgement. 62 tasks run on deterministic local sites scored from server state; 8 run on live GitHub, Wikipedia and JS Paint and are judged by a Claude Sonnet judge against API ground truth. Runs that hit a provider rate or usage limit were voided and rerun, never scored. Configurations still in progress and not shown: GPT-6 Astra high (13/70), GPT-6 Astra max (17/70), GPT-6 Astra medium (12/70), GPT-6 Astra xhigh (9/70), GPT-5.6 Luna high (2/70), GPT-5.6 Luna low (10/70), GPT-5.6 Luna max (3/70), GPT-5.6 Luna medium (8/70), GPT-5.6 Luna xhigh (8/70). [Task set](https://github.com/jshan9078/web-bench/blob/main/results/core_set.json), [discriminating set](https://github.com/jshan9078/web-bench/blob/main/results/validated_set.json), [per-run results](https://github.com/jshan9078/web-bench/tree/main/results).",
